    "TITLE": "General Taxonomy of Artifacts",
    "LEAD": "This platform organizes the vast diversity of artifacts that are part of human life — tools, machines, technical substances, informational systems, symbolic objects, and biotechnological devices — under a common classification framework inspired by biological taxonomy.",
    "WHAT_TITLE": "What is an artifact?",
    "WHAT_TEXT": "An entity produced through deliberate human intervention: it is not enough for something to be used; it must have been designed, modified, or created with a practical, technical, symbolic, or social purpose. A carved spoon, a book, a program, a medicine, or a domesticated plant can be artifacts in this sense.",
    "PROBLEM_TITLE": "What problem does this wiki solve?",
